---
import EdgeHead from '../../components/EdgeHead.astro';
import ToolNavigation from '../../components/ToolNavigation.astro';
// Isolated connected EDGE review preview.
---
<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>From a question to progress | EDGE</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/journey/journey.css"><EdgeHead title="From a question to progress | EDGE" description="A working brief for decisions, action and learning. AI suggestions are optional."/></head><body>
<div class="notice">AI suggestions are optional. Your brief stays editable. No automatic saving.</div>
<div class="shell"><ToolNavigation/>
<header><div class="eyebrow"><img src="/brand/edge-mark-on-navy.svg" width="32" height="32" alt="EDGE">A little clarity. A useful next step.</div><h1>Think it through.<br><span>Put it into practice<b class="full-stop">.</b></span></h1><div class="intro"><p>Start with something that matters to you. Compare your options, choose a direction and learn as you go.</p><p class="small">One connected brief. Four useful perspectives.<br>Start anywhere, go only as deep as you need.</p></div></header>
<section class="start" aria-label="Starting point"><div><span class="eyebrow">Try a fictional example</span><div class="choices"><button data-example="team">Launch a service</button><button data-example="student">Plan a student event</button><button data-example="personal">Make time to learn</button></div></div><button id="blank" class="quiet">Start with my own situation ↗</button></section>
<div class="journey-nav" role="tablist" aria-label="EDGE stages"></div>
<main class="workspace"><section class="editor"><div class="stage-top"><span id="step" class="eyebrow"></span><span id="origin" class="tag"></span></div><h2 id="heading" tabindex="-1"></h2><p id="description"></p><div role="group" id="approaches" class="approaches" aria-label="Decision approach"><button data-approach="compare" aria-pressed="true">Compare options</button><button data-approach="challenge" aria-pressed="false">Challenge my plan</button></div><div id="carry"></div><section class="assist"><div><strong>A second perspective, when useful.</strong><p>Only this stage and your selected context are sent to our server and OpenAI. Use anonymised details.</p></div><button id="suggest">Suggest improvements</button><button id="cancel-ai" hidden>Cancel</button><p id="ai-status" role="status"></p><div id="suggestions"></div></section><form id="fields"></form><div class="actions"><button id="next" class="primary"></button><span id="stage-status" class="small" role="status"></span></div></section>
<aside><div class="orbit" aria-hidden="true"><span>E</span><i></i></div><div class="eyebrow">Your working brief</div><h3 id="brief-title">A new possibility.</h3><p class="small">Your words stay editable. Suggestions and assumptions stay separate from confirmed decisions.</p><div id="ledger"></div><details><summary>How this working brief works</summary><p>Examples are written illustrations, not evidence of real outcomes. AI suggestions are separate drafts that you choose whether to use. Your edits stay in this tab until it is closed or refreshed. Export a copy to keep them.</p><p>Moving between stages does not approve a decision. At each handoff you choose which details to carry forward.</p></details><button id="practice-handoff">Practise a conversation about this</button><p class="small">Choose shared context first. Your brief is kept temporarily in this tab so you can return.</p><div class="exports"><button id="export">Download working brief</button><button id="copy">Copy summary</button></div><p id="export-status" role="status" class="small"></p><img class="dare" src="/brand/dare.png" width="140" alt="DARE by democratising.ai"></aside></main>
<footer><span>EDGE, created by Adrian Watkins</span><a href="/tools/before-you-send">Just need to review a message? Before You Send ↗</a></footer></div>
<dialog id="handoff" aria-labelledby="handoff-title"><form method="dialog"><button class="close" aria-label="Close handoff">×</button></form><span class="eyebrow">Bring the useful parts with you</span><h2 id="handoff-title">Review before you move.</h2><p>Select what belongs in the next stage. Nothing becomes a confirmed fact simply because it moves forward.</p><div id="handoff-items"></div><button id="confirm" class="primary">Carry selected details forward</button></dialog><dialog id="practice-dialog" aria-labelledby="practice-title"><form method="dialog"><button class="close" aria-label="Close practice handoff">×</button></form><span class="eyebrow">Choose what the counterpart knows</span><h2 id="practice-title">Share only the useful context.</h2><p>Selected wording becomes the shared scenario. Keep private goals, limits and alternatives out. You can edit the scenario again before starting.</p><div id="practice-items"></div><p id="practice-status" role="status"></p><button id="open-practice" class="primary">Continue to practice</button></dialog><script is:inline src="/journey/journey.js"></script></body></html>
